                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Internal medicine(II) is the medical specialty dealing with the diagnosis, treatment and prevention of diseases in adult. It is a fundamental curriculum of clinical disciplines and the education of internists and about research. The course is composed of：</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Module 1 Disorders of the Kidney and Urinary Tract</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Module 2 Disorders of hemotologic System</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Module 3 Endocrinology and Metabolism</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Module 4 Disorders of the Immune System, Connective Tissue, and Joints</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Module 5 Poisoning and Diseases of Critical Care Medicine</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
